{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"These are **industry conventions, not universal legal safe harbors**:\n\n- **$0.01 per share** commonly distinguishes errors affecting the published, cent-rounded NAV and informs NAV adjustment and fund-level remediation.\n- **0.5% of NAV** commonly serves as a materiality benchmark for reprocessing NAV-based transactions and compensating affected investors. It is not permission to ignore smaller errors.\n\nCorrection depends on applicable law and SEC guidance, the fund’s board-approved valuation/error-correction policies, governing documents and agreements, and the actual losses and affected parties. An administrator should calculate the correct NAV, assess fund and transactor harm separately, escalate appropriately, and document remediation—not mechanically apply either threshold.\n\n**Worth knowing:** For ETFs, creation/redemption transactions require particular analysis; secondary-market trades occur at market prices and are not automatically repriced because NAV was wrong."}}
